  10:     Stagger the two horizontal input regions onto a larger maroon separator canvas.
  11: 
  12:     Input structure:
  13:     - The input is a rectangular grid with an even number of rows.
  14:     - The top half and bottom half are the two regions to preserve.
  15:     - Maroon is absent from the input and is used only as the new separator color.
  16: 
  17:     Rule:
  18:     - Create an output with one extra row and one extra column, filled with maroon.
  19:     - Copy the top half into the upper-left corner.
  20:     - Copy the bottom half one row below the top region and one column to the right.
  21: 
  22:     Key insight:
  23:     The output is not a recoloring of either region; it inserts an L-shaped maroon
  24:     gap by diagonally offsetting the lower half from the upper half.
  25:     """
